CWE: CWE-310
Function: {"purpose": "Determine the appropriate handshake MAC and PRF algorithm for TLS connections based on protocol version and cipher suite.", "security_relevant_behavior": "The function selects cryptographic algorithms for TLS handshake message authentication and key derivation. Incorrect selection could lead to cryptographic weaknesses or compatibility issues."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Remote attacker sends crafted traffic from a TLS 1.2 client.", "abstract_cause": "Incorrect protocol version check leads to wrong algorithm selection.", "detailed_cause": "The function used TLS1_get_version(s) >= TLS1_2_VERSION to check for TLS 1.2, but this comparison could incorrectly evaluate to true for protocol versions other than TLS 1.2, causing the wrong algorithm path to be taken.", "required_preconditions": ["TLS 1.2 client connection", "Specific cipher suite configuration"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Replace version range check with exact equality comparison against TLS 1.2 version constant.", "added_guards": ["Exact version equality check (s->method->version == TLS1_2_VERSION)"], "changed_operations": ["Changed from TLS1_get_version(s) >= TLS1_2_VERSION to s->method->version == TLS1_2_VERSION"], "post_fix_invariant": "The TLS 1.2-specific algorithm path is only taken when the actual protocol version is exactly TLS 1.2."}

CWE: CWE-119
Function: {"purpose": "Retrieve serialized session data from a TLS session object", "security_relevant_behavior": "Copies session data to a caller-provided buffer after checking buffer size"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Calling gnutls_session_get_data with a buffer smaller than required", "abstract_cause": "Ordering error in buffer size validation", "detailed_cause": "Buffer size check performed after overwriting the size output parameter", "required_preconditions": ["Nonstandard session resumption is performed", "Remote TLS server provides large SessionTicket"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Reorder operations to validate buffer size before modifying output parameters", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Moved *session_data_size = psession.size after buffer size check"], "post_fix_invariant": "Buffer size validation occurs before any output parameter modification"}

CWE: CWE-20
Function: {"purpose": "Manifest configuration defining exposed capabilities and interface permissions for Chrome's content browser service.", "security_relevant_behavior": "Controls which interfaces are exposed to renderer processes through the navigation:frame filter, potentially allowing web content to access privileged browser APIs."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "A remote attacker creates a crafted HTML page that triggers the web payments API on blob: or data: schemes.", "abstract_cause": "Excessive interface exposure to untrusted contexts.", "detailed_cause": "The manifest exposed certain ChromeOS-specific interfaces (crostini_upgrader::mojom::PageHandlerFactory) to renderer processes through the navigation:frame filter, which could be accessed via blob: or data: URLs in the web payments API.", "required_preconditions": ["Web payments API enabled", "Access to blob: or data: schemes", "ChromeOS environment (for the specific removed interface)"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Remove unnecessary interface exposure by deleting the crostini_upgrader::mojom::PageHandlerFactory from the exposed interface list.", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Removed one interface from ExposeInterfaceFilterCapability_Deprecated list"], "post_fix_invariant": "The crostini_upgrader interface is no longer exposed to renderer processes through the navigation:frame filter."}

CWE: CWE-200
Function: {"purpose": "Receive an L2TP-over-IPv6 message and copy relevant data to user space.", "security_relevant_behavior": "Fills a socket address structure (sockaddr_l2tpip6) with connection information when provided by the caller."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Local user makes a recvmsg or recvfrom system call on an L2TP-over-IPv6 socket.", "abstract_cause": "Uninitialized structure member.", "detailed_cause": "The l2tp_conn_id field of the sockaddr_l2tpip6 structure was not explicitly set before being returned to user space.", "required_preconditions": ["Local access to an L2TP-over-IPv6 socket."]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Initialize all fields of the returned socket address structure.", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Explicit initialization of l2tp_conn_id field to zero."], "post_fix_invariant": "All fields of the sockaddr_l2tpip6 structure returned to user space are explicitly initialized."}

CWE: CWE-200
Function: {"purpose": "Receive messages from an IUCV socket, handling different socket types (SOCK_SEQPACKET, SOCK_STREAM) and flags (MSG_PEEK, MSG_TRUNC).", "security_relevant_behavior": "The function copies data from kernel socket buffers to user space via msghdr and can include control messages with put_cmsg."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "A local user makes a crafted recvmsg or recvfrom system call on an IUCV socket.", "abstract_cause": "Kernel stack memory information leak.", "detailed_cause": "The msghdr structure passed from user space contains a field (msg_namelen) that is not initialized by the kernel function before being returned to user space.", "required_preconditions": ["Local user access", "Ability to call recvmsg/recvfrom on an IUCV socket"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Explicitly initialize the sensitive field in the user-provided structure before the function returns.", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Added initialization: msg->msg_namelen = 0; at the beginning of the function."], "post_fix_invariant": "The msg_namelen field of the msghdr structure is guaranteed to be zero when the function returns, preventing leakage of uninitialized kernel stack memory."}

CWE: CWE-20
Function: {"purpose": "Handle navigation events by updating content source tracking and managing rendering timeouts", "security_relevant_behavior": "Controls when stale rendered content is cleared after navigation, affecting UI spoofing vulnerability"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Navigation to a crafted HTML page", "abstract_cause": "Insufficiently quick clearing of stale rendered content", "detailed_cause": "Early return condition prevented timeout from starting when surface IDs remained unchanged", "required_preconditions": ["Surface synchronization enabled", "Old and new surface IDs equal after navigation"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Remove early return that skipped timeout initialization", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Removed conditional return based on surface ID comparison"], "post_fix_invariant": "Timeout always starts after navigation regardless of surface ID changes"}

CWE: CWE-20
Function: {"purpose": "Load a resource asynchronously for a MIME handler view container", "security_relevant_behavior": "Resource loading through service workers"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Service worker redirecting to a cross-origin PDF", "abstract_cause": "Missing service worker bypass for plugin resource requests", "detailed_cause": "Plugin resource requests went through service workers, allowing cross-origin data leakage", "required_preconditions": ["Service worker enabled", "Cross-origin PDF resource", "Embedded MIME handler view"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Configure request to bypass service workers", "added_guards": ["SetServiceWorkerMode(kNone)"], "changed_operations": ["Resource request configuration"], "post_fix_invariant": "Plugin resource requests skip service workers"}

CWE: CWE-20
Function: {"purpose": "Loads and manages image resources for HTML elements, handling different element types and loading scenarios.", "security_relevant_behavior": "Sets the request context for resource loading, which influences how content security policies are applied to different types of embedded content."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Loading an HTML page containing an <object> element with a crafted resource.", "abstract_cause": "Incorrect request context assignment for certain HTML elements during resource loading.", "detailed_cause": "The code failed to set the appropriate request context for <object> and <embed> elements, defaulting to a generic or incorrect context that didn't properly trigger CSP enforcement.", "required_preconditions": ["HTML page contains <object> or <embed> elements", "Content Security Policy is configured", "Resource loading occurs through ImageLoader"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Explicitly set correct request contexts for specific HTML element types to ensure proper CSP enforcement.", "added_guards": ["Explicit element type checks for <object> and <embed>"], "changed_operations": ["Added conditional logic to set WebURLRequest::kRequestContextObject for <object> elements", "Added conditional logic to set WebURLRequest::kRequestContextEmbed for <embed> elements"], "post_fix_invariant": "All resource requests from <object> and <embed> elements have their correct request context set, ensuring proper CSP evaluation."}

CWE: CWE-416
Function: {"purpose": "Determine the current profiling mode based on command-line switches and feature flags", "security_relevant_behavior": "Parses and validates user-provided mode strings from command-line arguments or feature configuration"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Processing a crafted PDF file", "abstract_cause": "Use-after-free leading to heap corruption", "detailed_cause": "The vulnerability was in PDFium, not in this specific function. This code change is unrelated to the CVE-2017-15411 vulnerability.", "required_preconditions": []}
Fix: {"strategy": "Extracted string-to-mode conversion logic into a separate function for better maintainability and error handling", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Replaced inline mode string comparisons with a call to ConvertStringToMode function"], "post_fix_invariant": "Mode validation logic is centralized in ConvertStringToMode"}

CWE: CWE-119
Function: {"purpose": "Opens a media device for streaming after checking origin permissions.", "security_relevant_behavior": "Passes parameters to a media manager function that opens devices."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Calling DoOpenDevice with crafted parameters.", "abstract_cause": "Incorrect parameter ordering in a function call.", "detailed_cause": "The page_request_id and requester_id parameters were swapped in the OpenDevice call.", "required_preconditions": ["Remote attacker can trigger DoOpenDevice", "Crafted HTML page can supply parameters"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Corrected parameter order in function call.", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Swapped positions of page_request_id and requester_id arguments"], "post_fix_invariant": "Parameters passed to OpenDevice match its expected signature."}

CWE: CWE-200
Function: {"purpose": "Receive messages from Bluetooth sockets", "security_relevant_behavior": "Copies data from kernel socket buffers to user space"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Local user makes recvmsg or recvfrom system call on Bluetooth socket", "abstract_cause": "Uninitialized kernel stack memory disclosure", "detailed_cause": "msg->msg_namelen field not initialized before potential early return", "required_preconditions": ["Local access", "Bluetooth socket available"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Initialize sensitive field before any code path that could return", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Moved msg->msg_namelen = 0 before skb_recv_datagram call"], "post_fix_invariant": "msg->msg_namelen always initialized before any return"}

CWE: CWE-20
Function: {"purpose": "Handles HTTP redirects during navigation, updating navigation state and performing security checks.", "security_relevant_behavior": "Validates redirect URLs for safety and authorization before proceeding with the redirected navigation."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "A navigation request is redirected to a URL that fails security policy checks.", "abstract_cause": "Incorrect error handling after a security check failure during redirect processing.", "detailed_cause": "When a redirect URL was denied by security policy (CanRedirectToURL or CanRequestURL), the code only reset the navigation request without displaying an error page, leaving the previous page in place.", "required_preconditions": ["A navigation request undergoes an HTTP redirect.", "The redirect target URL fails either the CanRedirectToURL check (general redirect safety) or the CanRequestURL check (process-specific authorization for non-browser-initiated navigations)."]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Replace the silent navigation reset with an explicit error page display for security policy failures.", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Replaced calls to 'frame_tree_node_->ResetNavigationRequest(false, true);' with calls to 'OnRequestFailedInternal' for the two security policy failure cases."], "post_fix_invariant": "When a redirect is denied by security policy, an error page is shown to the user instead of leaving the previous page displayed."}

CWE: CWE-20
Function: {"purpose": "IDN spoofing detection by mapping visually similar characters (confusables) to their ASCII equivalents to prevent URL bar spoofing.", "security_relevant_behavior": "The code defines a mapping from Unicode characters that resemble ASCII letters/digits to their ASCII equivalents. This mapping is used to detect when a domain name uses visually confusable characters to impersonate a legitimate domain."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "A remote attacker provides a crafted domain name containing specific Unicode characters that visually resemble ASCII characters but were not mapped by the spoof checker.", "abstract_cause": "Incomplete confusable character mapping allowed certain Unicode characters to bypass spoof detection.", "detailed_cause": "The mapping rules in 'extra_confusable_mapper_' did not include several Devanagari, Bengali, Gurmukhi, Gujarati, Oriya, Kannada, Tamil, and Thai digit characters that visually resemble ASCII digits (0-9).", "required_preconditions": ["The application renders the domain name in the URL bar (Omnibox).", "The domain name uses the unmapped confusable characters."]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Extend the existing confusable character mapping to include additional Unicode digit characters from multiple scripts that visually resemble ASCII digits.", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Extended the transliteration rules in 'extra_confusable_mapper_' to map additional Unicode digit characters to ASCII digits (o, q, u, 2, 3, 4, 8, 9)."], "post_fix_invariant": "The spoof checker now maps a more comprehensive set of visually confusable digit characters from multiple scripts to their ASCII equivalents."}

CWE: CWE-20
Function: {"purpose": "Execute browser commands based on command IDs, including platform-specific commands for macOS.", "security_relevant_behavior": "Handles a command (IDC_TOGGLE_JAVASCRIPT_APPLE_EVENTS) that controls whether JavaScript execution via Apple Events is allowed."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "A local attacker sends Apple Events to the browser process.", "abstract_cause": "Insufficient input validation/restriction for a platform-specific inter-process communication mechanism.", "detailed_cause": "The command handler for IDC_TOGGLE_JAVASCRIPT_APPLE_EVENTS directly toggled a user preference (prefs::kAllowJavascriptAppleEvents) without enforcing additional security checks or restrictions, allowing the preference to be set via Apple Events.", "required_preconditions": ["The application runs on macOS.", "The attacker has local access to the system.", "The browser is configured to accept Apple Events."]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Replace direct preference manipulation with a dedicated security-checking function.", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Replaced `prefs->SetBoolean(prefs::kAllowJavascriptAppleEvents, !prefs->GetBoolean(prefs::kAllowJavascriptAppleEvents))` with a call to `chrome::ToggleJavaScriptFromAppleEventsAllowed(browser_)`."], "post_fix_invariant": "Toggling the 'allow JavaScript from Apple Events' setting now requires passing through a centralized function that can enforce security policies."}

CWE: CWE-284
Function: {"purpose": "Test function that loads a URL and monitors download progress until completion", "security_relevant_behavior": "Reports error when total download size is non-positive"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Calling ReportError with a 64-bit integer argument", "abstract_cause": "Type mismatch in function argument", "detailed_cause": "ReportError expects int32_t parameter but receives int64_t", "required_preconditions": ["total_bytes_to_be_received <= 0"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Explicit type conversion to match expected parameter type", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Added static_cast<int32_t>() around total_bytes_to_be_received"], "post_fix_invariant": "ReportError receives properly typed argument"}

CWE: CWE-264
Function: {"purpose": "Check permissions for attaching perf events to tracepoints", "security_relevant_behavior": "Determines whether a user has sufficient privilege to enable function tracing via perf events"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Local user attempts to enable function tracing via perf events", "abstract_cause": "Incorrect permission check for function trace events", "detailed_cause": "The function trace permission check used perf_paranoid_kernel() instead of perf_paranoid_tracepoint_raw()", "required_preconditions": ["User has local access", "User runs crafted application", "perf_paranoid_kernel() returns false while perf_paranoid_tracepoint_raw() returns true"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Use consistent permission check for raw tracepoint access", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Replaced perf_paranoid_kernel() with perf_paranoid_tracepoint_raw() in function trace check"], "post_fix_invariant": "Function tracing requires the same raw tracepoint permission check as other raw tracepoint access"}

CWE: CWE-189
Function: {"purpose": "Parse MPEG-4 file format chunks recursively, handling various box types to extract media metadata and track information.", "security_relevant_behavior": "Processes untrusted MPEG-4 data from external sources, performing arithmetic operations on chunk sizes and memory allocations based on these values."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Processing a crafted MPEG-4 file containing a 'tx3g' chunk with a large chunk_size value.", "abstract_cause": "Integer overflow in buffer size calculation leading to insufficient memory allocation.", "detailed_cause": "When handling the 'tx3g' chunk type, the code calculates 'size + chunk_size' without checking if 'chunk_size' itself exceeds SIZE_MAX. The original check 'SIZE_MAX - chunk_size <= size' only protected against overflow when adding size and chunk_size, but didn't prevent chunk_size alone from exceeding SIZE_MAX.", "required_preconditions": ["The parser receives malicious MPEG-4 data", "The data contains a 'tx3g' chunk with chunk_size > SIZE_MAX"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Add an explicit check for chunk_size exceeding SIZE_MAX before performing the addition operation.", "added_guards": ["Check: (chunk_size > SIZE_MAX) before the existing overflow check"], "changed_operations": ["Modified the overflow validation from single check to two checks: first ensures chunk_size <= SIZE_MAX, then ensures addition won't overflow"], "post_fix_invariant": "Both chunk_size and the sum (size + chunk_size) are guaranteed not to exceed SIZE_MAX before buffer allocation."}

CWE: CWE-189
Function: {"purpose": "Parse sample-to-chunk mapping parameters from MP4 file format to correlate media samples with file chunks", "security_relevant_behavior": "Allocates memory based on a count value read from untrusted input without checking for integer overflow in the size calculation"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Processing crafted MP4 data containing a malicious sample-to-chunk count", "abstract_cause": "Integer overflow in memory allocation size calculation", "detailed_cause": "Multiplication of untrusted count (mNumSampleToChunkOffsets) by fixed element size (12 bytes for data validation, sizeof(SampleToChunkEntry) for allocation) without overflow check", "required_preconditions": ["Untrusted input source", "32-bit integer arithmetic", "Allocation based on multiplied size"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Add overflow check before memory allocation", "added_guards": ["Check if multiplication of count by element size exceeds maximum size_t value"], "changed_operations": ["Added overflow validation: SIZE_MAX / sizeof(SampleToChunkEntry) <= mNumSampleToChunkOffsets"], "post_fix_invariant": "Memory allocation size calculation is validated to not overflow before allocation"}

CWE: CWE-189
Function: {"purpose": "Deserialize a GraphicBuffer object from flattened data containing file descriptors and integer values.", "security_relevant_behavior": "Reads counts of file descriptors (numFds) and integers (numInts) from untrusted input, then allocates memory and copies data based on these counts."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Processing maliciously crafted flattened GraphicBuffer data with large numFds or numInts values.", "abstract_cause": "Integer overflow in size calculations leading to insufficient memory allocation.", "detailed_cause": "The values numFds and numInts from untrusted input were used without validation to calculate memory allocation size (sizeNeeded) and copy operations, allowing integer overflow in (10 + numInts) * sizeof(int) or similar calculations.", "required_preconditions": ["Attacker controls flattened GraphicBuffer data", "numFds or numInts values large enough to cause integer overflow"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Add bounds checking before using untrusted count values in calculations.", "added_guards": ["Check that numFds < maxNumber where maxNumber = UINT_MAX / sizeof(int)", "Check that numInts < (maxNumber - 10) to prevent overflow in (10 + numInts) calculation"], "changed_operations": ["Added validation of numFds and numInts against maximum safe values", "Added check for native_handle_create failure"], "post_fix_invariant": "numFds and numInts values are validated to prevent integer overflow before any size calculations or memory allocations."}

CWE: CWE-264
Function: {"purpose": "Determine if a process can ptrace or access sensitive information from another task", "security_relevant_behavior": "Checks credentials and dumpable status to authorize cross-process inspection"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Local user attempts to ptrace or access sensitive information from another process", "abstract_cause": "Incorrect dumpable status check allows bypass of intended restrictions", "detailed_cause": "The condition '!dumpable' incorrectly treats SUID_DUMP_ROOT as restrictive when it should be permissive", "required_preconditions": ["Target process has dumpable status SUID_DUMP_ROOT", "Attacker lacks ptrace capabilities"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Make dumpable check explicit about which states should restrict access", "added_guards": ["dumpable != SUID_DUMP_USER"], "changed_operations": ["Changed boolean negation to explicit value comparison"], "post_fix_invariant": "Only SUID_DUMP_USER dumpable status permits ptrace without capabilities"}

CWE: CWE-119
Function: {"purpose": "Construct an error response for unrecognized iSCSI parameters", "security_relevant_behavior": "Copies a user-provided key string into a fixed-size buffer within a heap-allocated structure"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Processing a long key parameter in an iSCSI error response", "abstract_cause": "Buffer overflow due to unbounded string copy", "detailed_cause": "Using strlen(key) + 1 as copy length without checking against destination buffer size", "required_preconditions": ["Key string length exceeds destination buffer size", "Key is provided by remote attacker"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Replace unbounded copy with bounded copy using destination buffer size", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["strncpy replaced with strlcpy", "Copy length changed from source-based to destination-based"], "post_fix_invariant": "Copy operations are bounded by destination buffer sizes"}

CWE: CWE-20
Function: {"purpose": "Process intra-coded macroblocks in H.264 video decoding, handling intra prediction modes and reconstruction for luma and chroma components.", "security_relevant_behavior": "The function processes intra prediction modes derived from bitstream data and uses them to predict pixel values. Invalid prediction mode values can lead to out-of-bounds array accesses when used as indices into prediction function tables."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Processing a crafted media file containing invalid intra prediction mode values.", "abstract_cause": "Missing bounds check on intra prediction mode index before using it to index into function pointer arrays.", "detailed_cause": "The intra prediction mode value derived from the bitstream is used directly as an index into arrays of function pointers (apf_intra_pred_luma_4x4, apf_intra_pred_luma_8x8, apf_intra_pred_chroma) without validation that the value falls within the valid range [0,8].", "required_preconditions": ["Maliciously crafted media file with invalid intra prediction mode values", "Decoder processes an intra-coded macroblock", "Intra prediction mode calculation produces out-of-range value"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Add explicit bounds clamping to ensure intra prediction mode values are within valid range before use.", "added_guards": ["Added CLIP3(0, 8, i1_intra_pred) calls to clamp prediction mode values to valid range [0,8]"], "changed_operations": ["Added bounds clamping for 4x4 intra prediction mode before array indexing", "Added bounds clamping for 8x8 intra prediction mode before array indexing"], "post_fix_invariant": "All intra prediction mode values used as array indices are guaranteed to be within the valid range [0,8]."}

CWE: CWE-119
Function: {"purpose": "Process DRM-protected media data by decrypting and potentially reformatting video content", "security_relevant_behavior": "Parses variable-length encoded data structures (NAL units) from untrusted input without sufficient bounds checking"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Processing a crafted media file containing maliciously constructed NAL unit length values", "abstract_cause": "Integer overflow in buffer offset calculation leading to out-of-bounds memory access", "detailed_cause": "Missing validation that arithmetic operations on buffer offsets (dstOffset + 4 + nalLength) do not overflow and remain within buffer bounds", "required_preconditions": ["Processing AVC/H.264 video content", "NAL fragmentation disabled (mWantsNALFragments false)", "Malformed NAL length values causing arithmetic overflow"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Add explicit integer overflow checks before buffer access operations", "added_guards": ["Check for overflow in dstOffset + 4", "Check for overflow in dstOffset + 4 + nalLength", "Verify resulting offset stays within buffer size"], "changed_operations": ["Replaced single bounds check with multi-step overflow validation", "Added buffer release on validation failure"], "post_fix_invariant": "All arithmetic operations on buffer offsets are checked for overflow before buffer access"}

CWE: CWE-264
Function: {"purpose": "Read data from a queue of media buffers", "security_relevant_behavior": "Accesses buffer memory using indices and offsets from queue entries without validation"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Processing a crafted queue entry with invalid buffer index or offset", "abstract_cause": "Missing bounds checking on buffer access", "detailed_cause": "The code used mBuffers.editItemAt(entry->mIndex) without validating that entry->mIndex is within mBuffers bounds, and accessed memory at entry->mOffset without validating the offset is within the buffer's size", "required_preconditions": ["Attacker controls or influences queue entry data", "Entry contains malicious mIndex or mOffset values", "Entry passes initial mIsCommand check"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Add bounds checks before buffer access", "added_guards": ["Check entry->mIndex < mBuffers.size()", "Check mem != NULL", "Check mem->size() >= copy", "Check mem->size() - copy >= entry->mOffset"], "changed_operations": ["Buffer access now validates index and offset before memcpy"], "post_fix_invariant": "Buffer index is validated against container size, and memory access offset is validated against buffer size before dereferencing"}

CWE: CWE-264
Function: {"purpose": "Demangle C++ symbol names for human-readable display in stack traces", "security_relevant_behavior": "Processes untrusted symbol names from applications through __cxa_demangle"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Processing a crafted symbol name from an untrusted application", "abstract_cause": "Unsafe processing of untrusted input through a complex parsing function", "detailed_cause": "__cxa_demangle called on attacker-controlled symbol names without validation", "required_preconditions": ["Attacker can influence symbol names in debuggable application", "debuggerd has elevated privileges"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Remove functionality rather than attempt to secure it", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Removed __cxa_demangle call entirely"], "post_fix_invariant": "Untrusted symbol names are never passed to complex parsing functions"}

CWE: CWE-200
Function: {"purpose": "Allocate and register a buffer header for use by an OMX component", "security_relevant_behavior": "Accepts an externally provided buffer pointer and size, associates them with internal structures without validation"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Calling useBuffer with a size parameter smaller than the port's configured buffer size", "abstract_cause": "Missing validation of input parameter against internal requirements", "detailed_cause": "The function accepted a size parameter smaller than port->mDef.nBufferSize, allowing undersized buffers to be registered", "required_preconditions": ["Component is in OMX_StateLoaded state or port is disabled", "Port buffer count hasn't reached maximum"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Add early validation check before buffer header creation", "added_guards": ["size >= port->mDef.nBufferSize"], "changed_operations": ["Added parameter validation with error return"], "post_fix_invariant": "All registered buffers have size at least port->mDef.nBufferSize"}

CWE: CWE-119
Function: {"purpose": "Decode a Base64-encoded string into binary data", "security_relevant_behavior": "Writes decoded bytes to an output buffer of predetermined size"}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Processing a Base64 string with padding", "abstract_cause": "Missing bounds check before writing first decoded byte", "detailed_cause": "The first output byte write occurred without checking if the output buffer had sufficient space", "required_preconditions": ["Input string length is multiple of 4", "Input contains padding characters ('=')", "Calculated output length is insufficient for all write operations"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Add missing bounds check for first output byte write", "added_guards": ["Bounds check before writing the first decoded byte"], "changed_operations": ["Added conditional check 'if (j < outLen)' before 'out[j++] = (accum >> 16)'"], "post_fix_invariant": "All buffer writes are guarded by bounds checks against the calculated output length"}

CWE: CWE-476
Function: {"purpose": "Load EDID firmware data for a display connector by parsing a comma-separated list of firmware specifications, matching against connector names.", "security_relevant_behavior": "Duplicates a firmware string for parsing without checking if the memory allocation succeeded."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "Calling kstrdup with insufficient memory available.", "abstract_cause": "Missing null check after a memory allocation.", "detailed_cause": "The return value of kstrdup was not checked for NULL before being dereferenced.", "required_preconditions": ["edid_firmware[0] is not '\\0'", "kstrdup returns NULL due to memory allocation failure"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Add an explicit null check after the allocation and return an error code on failure.", "added_guards": ["if (!fwstr) return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);"], "changed_operations": [], "post_fix_invariant": "If kstrdup fails, the function returns an error pointer without proceeding to use the null pointer."}

CWE: CWE-399
Function: {"purpose": "Construct a netlink message containing network interface information for user-space consumption.", "security_relevant_behavior": "The function copies kernel data structures to user-space buffers without ensuring all fields are initialized, potentially leaking uninitialized kernel stack memory."}
Cause and trigger: {"triggering_action": "A local user crafts an application that triggers the rtnl_fill_ifinfo function to retrieve network interface information.", "abstract_cause": "Uninitialized stack memory containing sensitive kernel data is copied to user-space.", "detailed_cause": "A structure (ifla_vf_info) declared on the stack is partially initialized before being passed to a driver callback. If the callback fails, uninitialized fields (specifically the mac array) remain in the structure and are subsequently copied to the user-space message buffer.", "required_preconditions": ["Local user access", "Ability to trigger netlink interface queries", "Presence of SR-IOV capable drivers that may fail the ndo_get_vf_config callback"]}
Fix: {"strategy": "Explicitly initialize sensitive fields of the stack-allocated structure before potential use.", "added_guards": [], "changed_operations": ["Added memset to zero the mac field of the ifla_vf_info structure before the driver callback"], "post_fix_invariant": "All fields of the ifla_vf_info structure are explicitly initialized before being copied to user-space buffers, regardless of driver callback success."}

CWE: CWE-190
